 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Boundary Handling:** The iteration loop extends from `-1` to `CHUNK_SIZE + 1` to ensure quads on the chunk edges are generated, requiring neighbor checks to handle out-of-bounds coordinates correctly [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Degenerate Vertices:** If a corner has no incident edges crossing the surface, the smoothing formula divides by zero; a fallback to the raw integer position is required [G].
-*   **Precision:** Using floating-point midpoints can introduce small artifacts; consistent data types should be maintained throughout the pipeline [G].
+*   **Boundary Check:** The `FindFeaturePoints` kernel skips voxels where $x+1 \ge Size.x$, $y+1 \ge Size.y$, or $z+1 \ge Size.z$ to avoid accessing out-of-bounds neighbor voxels [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Boundary Handling:** The iteration loop extends from -1 to `CHUNK_SIZE + 1` to ensure quads on the chunk edges are generated, requiring neighbor checks to handle out-of-bounds or adjacent chunk data correctly via `IsInsideChunk` [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Division by Zero:** In `InverseLerp`, if $a == b$, the function returns 0 to prevent division by zero [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(V)$, where $V$ is the number of voxels in the chunk, as each voxel face is processed once and smoothing requires checking 12 incident edges per vertex [G].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(F)$, where $F$ is the number of surface faces, storing one vertex per smoothed corner and two triangles per face [G].
-*   **Strengths:** Produces a smoother surface than naive voxel meshing or standard Marching Cubes without the complexity of topological sorting or complex lookup tables [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** No culling of internal faces or optimization of vertex sharing across chunks; generates duplicate vertices at chunk boundaries if processed independently; performance degrades with high-resolution chunks due to per-vertex smoothing calculations [G].
-*   **When to use:** When visual smoothness is prioritized over mesh optimization and chunk boundaries are handled separately or merged later [G].
-*   **When not to use:** When memory efficiency or draw call reduction is critical, as it lacks vertex deduplication and culling [G].
